From 1d7bf4ec712ed520adb8aabec72c921658b95aca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James-Delgado <jado650@berkeley.edu>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 11:22:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] qwen-metal P6-2: Phase 6 parity bench for llama.swiftui
 (post-sample per-token timestamps, completion_init prefill bracket,
 generated-token caps + n_ctx 4096, loop timeline, SoC fields, exports)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stacked on the P0A-1 patches (97e552a, bceddff); base b9999/47c78692;
checkpoint (locally converted Q4_K_M GGUF) unchanged. See qwen-metal
docs/phases/phase-6.md D1/D2/D4/D9 and DECISIONS.md 2026-09-26 (P6-2).

LibLlama.swift (LlamaContext):
- token_available_ns: monotonic host time taken right after
  llama_sampler_sample returns token k. The sampler reads logits via
  llama_get_logits_ith, which calls ctx->synchronize() first
  (src/llama-context.cpp), so the stamp is a backend-completion mark;
  decode tok/s of record = 384 / (t512 - t128); the EOG token gets no
  stamp (not a generated token).
- prefill span = completion_init start (before tokenize) -> first sample
  returned = tokenize + one llama_decode over the prompt batch + first
  sample (spec D1). llama_decode's return is an async enqueue on Metal
  (the P0A-1 finding): the enqueue mark is recorded and labeled, never
  reported as prefill.
- caps: n_gen_max caps GENERATED tokens — burst 640 new tokens
  (= qwen-metal burstMaxNewTokens; Phase 0 capped 640 TOTAL), loop =
  n_ctx - n_prompt derived at completion_init so a generation resets
  exactly at the context fill; n_len derived from it; a defensive guard
  stops at n_ctx (a failed decode can no longer spin). Stop reasons in
  the qwen-metal vocabulary: eos | contextFull | maxNewTokens |
  stopRequested. Operator stop is honored at the token boundary after
  token k is available and before its decode is enqueued; the flag is
  per completion (cleared in clear()).
- n_ctx 2048 -> 4096: the pinned regenerate policy resets on the 4K
  context fill (PLAN); qwen-metal contextCap and the MLX loop cap are
  4096. KV allocation grows accordingly — the Phase 6 phys_footprint row
  for llama.cpp will differ from Phase 0's 307 MB for this reason too
  (stated, not hidden).

LlamaState.swift / ContentView.swift:
- P6 panel: prompt picker (bundled rendered prompts, parse_special=true
  — the P0A-1 pin), P6 Burst, P6 Loop / Stop (report), operator fields
  (battery health, SoC start, SoC end, cold/warm, round), Copy export /
  Copy JSON / Copy output. The token loop runs detached (no main-actor
  hop per token; no per-token UI — the P0A-1 lesson).
- exports: text of record (harness/checkpoint/validation lines,
  health and SoC as SEPARATE fields, programmatic UIDevice.batteryLevel
  as the labeled cross-check, task_info phys_footprint as a labeled
  cross-check, prefill span, decode rate overall + window, per-
  generation `gen N:` lines, cumulative tokens / sum wall / cycle wall)
  and the JSON timeline (schema qwen-metal-timeline/1-external, engine
  llama-swiftui). llama.cpp's own prompt counts are recorded against
  the counts on record (92 / 852; HF 84 / 852) — a tokenizer
  difference, reported as pinned.
- Metal API validation OFF: the shared scheme already carries
  enableGPUValidationMode="1" (= Disabled) from upstream; recorded in
  the export.

Build-verified: xcodebuild -scheme llama.swiftui -destination
generic/platform=iOS -configuration Release CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY="" -> BUILD SUCCEEDED. Never run for numbers by
agents.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
